2026-05-02  Karl Berry  <karl@freefriends.org>

	* scripts/build-tl.sh: try gcc15 per Bruno:
	https://tug.org/pipermail/tlbuild/2026q2/005996.html

2026-04-29  Karl Berry  <karl@freefriends.org>

	* scripts/build-tl.sh: always show build?*.log.

	* workflows/main.yml: switch to freebsd 14.4 (the current 14.x)
	https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeBSD_version_history#Version_history
	since a) 13.5 [the last 13.x] will be unsupported as of tomorrow,
	and b) we want to use gcc-15, since gcc-14 has only partial
	support for C23, which is worse than no support at all.
	(See luatex/ChangeLog and ustring.c.) Suggestion from Bruno:
	https://tug.org/pipermail/tlbuild/2026q2/005996.html
	
	14.4 will also be unsupported by the time we release TL27,
	but maybe there is nothing better to do. Neither building on
	unsupported versions nor constantly churning the build os seem
	good, but it seems there are no other options.

